# Chip Estimate Integrity — Phase C: Physical-hours concierge gate (CORE)
#
# ACCEPTANCE CONTRACT (locked before Phase C implementation edits)
# C1 GIVEN a local-move scope and active mover rate cards, WHEN the largest
#    positive crew size advertised across all active vendors is evaluated using
#    unrounded physical work hours, THEN <= 6.0 routes to instant comparison and
#    > 6.0 routes to concierge. Drive time and price never affect this gate.
# C2 GIVEN an active vendor whose card has no positive-rate crew capable of <= 6.0
#    physical hours, WHEN PricingEngine estimates that card, THEN it returns nil;
#    it never falls back to an over-ceiling quote. Zero/nonpositive rates are not
#    available crews.
# C3 GIVEN an instant estimate, WHEN its locked why-line is emitted, THEN the
#    selected crew's unrounded physical hours are <= 6.0 by construction. Tests
#    assert the invariant at the 6.0 boundary and immediately above it.
# C4 GIVEN a local move above the global largest-crew ceiling, WHEN comparison is
#    prepared, THEN quoteRequest=true, vendor cards are absent, and the existing
#    concierge card renders exactly "This is a big one." and "Big moves deserve
#    a hand-built quote — we'll have yours within a day." A simulator screenshot
#    captures the card. Long-distance gating remains intact.
# C5 GIVEN the repository and built app, WHEN the phase is audited, THEN there is
#    no bigMoveCubicFeetGate or other cube threshold. CORE tests, simulator tests,
#    a fresh-context validator, and walked hub-file diffs pass. No deploy occurs.
